 "sections": [
  {
   "name": "The Belt That Can Destroy Your Engine",
   "lines": [
    [
     "c20_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "One belt can *wreck* your engine",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "wow",
      "prop": {
       "type": "timing",
       "snap": true
      }
     },
     "There is a belt inside many engines that, if it snaps, can destroy the engine in a second."
    ],
    [
     "c20_2",
     {
      "label": "job",
      "head": "The *timing belt*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "timing"
      }
     },
     "The timing belt links the crankshaft to the camshafts, keeping the pistons and valves perfectly in step."
    ],
    [
     "c20_3",
     {
      "label": "half",
      "head": "The cams turn at *half* speed",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "timing"
      }
     },
     "The camshaft turns once for every two turns of the crank, because each valve opens once every four strokes."
    ],
    [
     "c20_4",
     {
      "label": "valves",
      "head": "Cams push the *valves*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "engine4",
       "speed": 1.4
      }
     },
     "Lobes on the camshaft push the valves open at exactly the right moment."
    ],
    [
     "c20_5",
     {
      "label": "snap",
      "head": "If it snaps: *crunch*",
      "pose": "facepalm",
      "face": "sad",
      "prop": {
       "type": "timing",
       "snap": true
      }
     },
     "In many engines, called interference engines, a snapped belt lets pistons smash into open valves."
    ],
    [
     "c20_6",
     {
      "label": "cost",
      "head": "A *cheap* job vs a big bill",
      "pose": "shrug",
      "face": "worried",
      "prop": {
       "type": "versus",
       "a": {
        "t": "REPLACE ON TIME",
        "big": "cheap",
        "sub": "planned service"
       },
       "b": {
        "t": "BELT SNAPS",
        "big": "costly",
        "sub": "engine damage"
       },
       "win": "a"
      }
     },
     "Replacing the belt on schedule is far cheaper than rebuilding a wrecked engine."
    ],
    [
     "c20_7",
     {
      "label": "when",
      "head": "Check your *interval*",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "think",
      "prop": {
       "type": "checklist",
       "items": [
        [
         "Find the interval in your manual",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Belt or chain? Ask",
         true
        ],
        [
         "Replace the water pump too",
         true
        ]
       ]
      }
     },
     "Many belts are due somewhere around sixty to a hundred thousand miles, or a set number of years. Timing chains usually last much longer."
    ],
    [
     "c20_8",
     {
      "label": "takeaway",
      "head": "Do not *skip* the belt",
      "pose": "thumbs",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "timing"
      }
     },
     "If your engine has a timing belt, do not skip it. It is one service that can save the whole engine."
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
